      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/KrasimirKralev/clx\n\n### Category\n\nPython\n\n### Project Title\n\nclx: switch AI coding accounts without restarting\n\n### Project Description\n\nclx is a Linux launcher for Anthropic's coding CLI. It starts each session on whichever of your own Pro/Max accounts has the most usage left. At its 5-hour or weekly limit, clx moves the running session to your next account without a restart.\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Unlike switchers that pick an account only at launch, clx also moves a session that is already running. The conversation, background tasks and subagents carry on; only the login used by the next request changes.\n- At launch it compares every window the server reports (5-hour, weekly and per-model) and picks the account with the most room.\n- One standard-library Python file, a bash hook and an installer. SECURITY.md lists every file it writes and the one request it makes, and `--uninstall` removes it.\n- It is for accounts that are all yours. The README has a \"Use it within Anthropic's terms\" section; sharing an account is forbidden.\n\nI'm the author of clx.\n\n### Example Code\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/KrasimirKralev/clx/releases/latest/download/clx.tar.gz | tar xz\n./clx/install.sh\ncm-login work you@work.example   # log in a second account, named work\nclx --status                     # every account, its usage, and which one clx would pick\nclx                              # start on the account with the most room\n```\n\n### Screenshots or Demo Videos\n\n![clx --status and a session moving between accounts](https://github.com/KrasimirKralev/clx/raw/main/docs/demo.svg)\n",
